what you really, really want ♪

11:49.780 --> 11:52.345
♪ I'll tell you want I want,
what I really, really want... ♪

11:53.881 --> 11:55.681
All right, Tom, if you
want to be young these days,

11:55.716 --> 11:58.583
you gotta do a wicked
awesome GoPro skate video.

12:14.025 --> 12:17.025
♪ I can't stand it ♪

12:17.061 --> 12:19.025
♪ I know you planned it ♪

12:19.061 --> 12:20.927
♪ I'm-a set it straight,
this Watergate ♪

12:20.963 --> 12:23.729
♪ I can't stand rocking
when I'm in here ♪

12:23.764 --> 12:26.897
♪ Because your crystal ball
ain't so crystal clear ♪

12:26.932 --> 12:30.032
♪ So while you sit back
and wonder why ♪

12:30.068 --> 12:32.367
♪ I got this ...
thorn in my side ♪

12:32.402 --> 12:35.635
♪ Oh, my God, it's a mirage ♪

12:35.670 --> 12:37.336
♪ I'm tellin' y'all
it's sabotage... ♪

12:52.079 --> 12:53.244
Bear Scares,

12:53.279 --> 12:55.478
<i>Latvia's number-one
bear prank show.</i>

12:55.513 --> 12:58.714
<i>Now available in region 3 DVD.</i>

13:01.717 --> 13:03.984
All right, Chris, nothing's
gotten that ring out yet.

13:04.019 --> 13:06.050
That's why we brought
you to this fast-food

13:06.086 --> 13:07.485
roast beef restaurant.

13:07.520 --> 13:09.986
Uh, yeah, I'll take
the Angus steak melt.

13:10.021 --> 13:11.687
I'm sorry, are you here
to poop something out?

13:11.723 --> 13:12.887
Yes.

13:12.923 --> 13:14.922
Okay, this line is just
for regular diners.

13:14.957 --> 13:16.222
You need to get
in that line.

13:18.626 --> 13:20.658
Excuse me, is this the line
for people who need

13:20.693 --> 13:21.726
to puke something up?

13:21.761 --> 13:23.526
I think this is
just the poop line.

13:25.129 --> 13:26.894
Cheers.

13:26.930 --> 13:29.896
You know what restaurant
we're talking about.

13:33.233 --> 13:34.932
Ah, almost time
for the news.

13:34.967 --> 13:35.933
Mind if I join you?

13:35.968 --> 13:37.267
I thought you
hated the news.

13:37.302 --> 13:39.402
Developing story:
I like it now.

13:40.770 --> 13:42.470
Okay.

13:42.505 --> 13:45.038
Good evening, Quahog,
I'm Dallas Portland.

13:45.073 --> 13:46.305
And I'm T-Homie...

13:46.340 --> 13:49.806
with the news
in your mouth!

13:49.842 --> 13:51.508
What the hell's he doing?

13:51.543 --> 13:53.042
He's crushing it.

13:53.077 --> 13:56.243
Okay, Tom, uh,
our top story tonight:

13:56.279 --> 13:58.711
a burst water pipe
in the pediatric unit

13:58.747 --> 14:01.079
of Quahog General
results in the tragic

14:01.115 --> 14:03.713
drowning deaths
of four children and one nurse.

14:03.750 --> 14:05.482
News bomb!

14:05.517 --> 14:06.749
I know what you're
thinking, right?

14:06.784 --> 14:08.050
"He's so random."

14:08.085 --> 14:09.217
Boy, I never realized

14:09.252 --> 14:11.652
how young and hip
Tom Tucker is.

14:11.687 --> 14:14.220
Dallas Portland should just
pack it up and go home.

14:14.255 --> 14:15.487
What are you talking about?

14:15.522 --> 14:16.688
Wait, wait, quiet, quiet.

14:16.723 --> 14:19.055
Tom's about to tattoo
the word, "Coachella"

14:19.090 --> 14:20.323
on the bridge of his nose.

14:20.358 --> 14:21.590
Is that a thing?

14:21.625 --> 14:23.358
Uh, I don't know, Grandma,
sit back and wa--

14:24.661 --> 14:25.625
He got his eye!
Oh, God!

14:25.661 --> 14:26.893
What's wrong
with you, Dallas?

14:26.928 --> 14:29.328
Never seen a guy so
young and cool before?

14:30.363 --> 14:31.461
Tumblr!

14:33.432 --> 14:35.163
I've just received
some breaking news.

14:35.198 --> 14:38.198
Channel Five News anchor
Tom Tucker has been relieved

14:38.234 --> 14:40.400
of his duties,
effective immediately.

14:40.435 --> 14:42.402
Holy crap! They fired him?

14:42.437 --> 14:43.436
Oh, my God!

14:43.470 --> 14:45.469
Oh, well, now
back to my life.

14:50.940 --> 14:51.839
Bear Scares

14:51.875 --> 14:52.973
<i>will be back after message</i>

14:53.008 --> 14:54.574
<i>from state-run industry.</i>

14:54.610 --> 14:55.775
<i>Shirt.gov,</i>

14:55.810 --> 14:56.941
<i>shirt.gov,</i>

14:56.977 --> 14:59.843
<i>is only place
to get your shirt.</i>

15:05.822 --> 15:07.288
Peter, you were
the one who told

15:07.323 --> 15:10.023
Tom Tucker to try
all that nonsense on TV?

15:10.058 --> 15:12.590
You realize you cost
that man his job.

15:12.626 --> 15:13.858
Well, how was
I supposed to know?

15:13.893 --> 15:16.293
Katie Couric went on TV
and stuck a tube up her butt

15:16.328 --> 15:17.393
and they threw her a parade.

15:17.428 --> 15:19.027
That was a colonoscopy!

15:19.061 --> 15:20.761
This is kind of
your fault, you know.

15:20.796 --> 15:22.028
I mean, you're the
one who was drooling

15:22.063 --> 15:23.296
over that Dallas Portland.

15:23.331 --> 15:25.163
I was just trying to get
that guy off the air.

15:25.199 --> 15:26.931
Peter, that's ridiculous.

15:26.966 --> 15:29.866
He's just some pretty boy
who doesn't mean anything.

15:29.901 --> 15:31.933
<i>It's like when you watch
Mad Men for that chick</i>

15:31.968 --> 15:33.368
you said was like a fat me.

15:33.403 --> 15:35.336
I said a young, fat you.

15:35.372 --> 15:38.103
The point is,
you've ruined that man's life.

15:38.138 --> 15:39.571
You're right.

15:39.606 --> 15:40.671
Poor Tom.

15:40.706 --> 15:42.439
Thanks to me,
he's fallen even

15:42.475 --> 15:44.207
further than Charlie Rose.

15:44.242 --> 15:46.708
<i>Today on CBS This Morning,
we'll be talking about</i>

15:46.744 --> 15:48.776
how much sleep you need
to not be drunk

15:48.811 --> 15:50.477
from the night before.

15:50.512 --> 15:51.844
That's not what
we're talking about.

15:51.879 --> 15:53.711
<i>That's what I'm
talking about.</i>

15:57.316 --> 15:58.881
I don't know
what else to do.

15:58.916 --> 16:00.081
We've tried everything.

16:00.117 --> 16:01.750
Brian, the jeweler
closes at 6:00.

16:01.785 --> 16:03.651
You don't have much time left
to return that ring.

16:03.686 --> 16:04.651
You're right.

16:04.686 --> 16:06.018
Well, we have no choice.

16:06.053 --> 16:08.053
We'll just have to take
a bumpy ride to the mall

16:08.088 --> 16:09.320
and hope for a miracle.

16:09.355 --> 16:11.421
You know, Brian,
this wouldn't have happened

16:11.456 --> 16:12.855
if you were just
honest with women

16:12.890 --> 16:14.356
and had an ounce
of integrity.

16:14.392 --> 16:15.556
Don't pull rank on me.

16:15.592 --> 16:17.724
You ate a ring,
you worthless tub of crap.

16:17.760 --> 16:18.724
Yeah?

16:18.760 --> 16:19.992
Well, who's gonna be
fishing through

16:20.028 --> 16:22.794
a tub of crap soon,
you unemployed buttmunch?

16:22.829 --> 16:24.727
Whoa, whoa,
let's calm down, guys.

16:24.763 --> 16:27.195
Shut up,
you unemployed buttmunch!

16:27.231 --> 16:29.598
Okay, he found
a burn he likes.

16:35.969 --> 16:37.467
What the hell do you want?

16:37.503 --> 16:38.602
I'm here to say...

16:38.637 --> 16:40.636
I'm sorry about
what happened.

16:40.672 --> 16:42.071
Let me make it up to you.

16:42.106 --> 16:43.937
I'm the one who made
you lose your job.

16:43.973 --> 16:45.239
I'll find you a new one.

16:45.274 --> 16:46.273
Don't bother.

16:46.308 --> 16:47.406
I'm washed up.

16:47.441 --> 16:49.940
Everyone saw what I did,
and besides, I...

16:49.976 --> 16:51.842
I can't do anything else.

16:51.878 --> 16:53.943
I was born to be a newsman.

16:53.979 --> 16:56.277
This just out: me!

16:56.313 --> 16:57.945
That-that happened?

16:57.981 --> 16:59.112
Is that for real?

16:59.148 --> 17:00.547
That's nuts, but still,

17:00.582 --> 17:02.315
I-I want to help you
get back on your feet.

17:02.350 --> 17:03.315
Go home, Peter.

17:03.350 --> 17:04.582
You've already done enough.

17:04.618 --> 17:06.083
Thanks to you,
it's over for me,

17:06.118 --> 17:07.850
like Billy Zane.

17:07.886 --> 17:08.950
Billy, you're through.

17:08.986 --> 17:10.519
You haven't done
anything in ten years.

17:10.554 --> 17:11.786
Yes, I have.

17:11.821 --> 17:13.887
I was in those electronic
cigarette commercials.

17:13.922 --> 17:15.254
That was Stephen Dorff.

17:15.289 --> 17:16.989
Aw.

17:21.193 --> 17:22.958
How we doing on time?
Less than a minute.

17:22.994 --> 17:24.259
How you feeling, Chris?

17:24.294 --> 17:26.694
No different, except I have
to poop from all this running.

17:26.729 --> 17:27.728
What? That's great!

17:27.762 --> 17:28.928
There's a bathroom
down that hall!

17:28.963 --> 17:30.629
No time!
They're closing the gate!

17:41.237 --> 17:42.202
<i>Hey, Shelby.</i>

17:42.237 --> 17:43.369
<i>Brian?</i>

17:43.404 --> 17:45.237
<i>It's coming!</i>

17:45.273 --> 17:47.371
<i>Oh, my God!</i>

17:47.406 --> 17:49.339
<i>Yes, um, I'd like to make
a return, please...</i>

17:49.374 --> 17:51.474
<i>and maybe take you to dinner?</i>

17:51.509 --> 17:54.375
<i>Brian, I don't care
that I was diarrhea'd on.</i>

17:54.410 --> 17:56.909
<i>I care that you weren't honest.</i>

17:56.944 --> 17:58.777
<i>I care that
I was diarrhea'd on.</i>

17:58.813 --> 18:00.945
<i>I care a great deal.</i>

18:05.882 --> 18:08.115
Sorry I let you down, Tom.

18:08.150 --> 18:09.616
Oh, my God, look!

18:09.652 --> 18:10.783
Up on the roof!

18:12.653 --> 18:13.919
Holy crap!

18:13.954 --> 18:16.320
Doritos Tacos is only
for a limited time?

18:17.356 --> 18:18.787
And oh, no!

18:18.823 --> 18:21.055
Tom Tucker's gonna jump!

18:27.327 --> 18:28.893
Tom, I got here as
fast as I could.

18:28.929 --> 18:30.627
So-so, what's-what's
going on?

18:30.663 --> 18:31.762
It's over for me, Peter.

18:31.797 --> 18:33.662
If I can't anchor
the local news,

18:33.697 --> 18:35.297
I have no reason to live.

18:35.332 --> 18:37.397
Look, Tom, Tom, before
you do anything crazy,

18:37.432 --> 18:38.832
you should know one thing:

18:38.867 --> 18:41.533
I have that exact
same bathrobe.

18:41.569 --> 18:43.633
Hey, Tom, the camera's
gonna be on you in a second.

18:43.669 --> 18:45.202
Before you jump,
could you just hand me

18:45.237 --> 18:47.837
this microphone, like you're
passing me the torch?

18:47.872 --> 18:49.337
What the hell
are you doing here?

18:49.373 --> 18:50.337
What am I doing?

18:50.373 --> 18:51.839
Getting an interview
with a crazed jumper

18:51.874 --> 18:52.905
on the brink of suicide.

18:52.941 --> 18:54.006
This is huge.

18:54.042 --> 18:55.640
Wait a second.

18:55.676 --> 18:57.042
You heard wrong, Dallas.

18:57.077 --> 18:59.242
There's a jumper here,
but it ain't Tom.

18:59.277 --> 19:00.543
It's me.
What?!

19:00.579 --> 19:01.543
That's right.

19:01.579 --> 19:03.044
Tom was just trying
to talk me down,

19:03.079 --> 19:05.011
and if there's
a news story here,

19:05.047 --> 19:08.013
the only one I'm giving
it to is Tom Tucker.

19:08.049 --> 19:10.248
Here.

19:10.283 --> 19:11.915
Roll it.

19:13.119 --> 19:14.083
Good evening, Quahog.

19:14.119 --> 19:15.650
This is Tom Tucker
atop a roof,

19:15.686 --> 19:18.852
where a local crazy person
is preparing to end it all.

19:18.887 --> 19:19.854
Bonnie!

19:19.888 --> 19:22.054
Tom Tucker's back on the news!

19:22.090 --> 19:23.355
Oh, here you are.

19:23.391 --> 19:24.355
Tom Tucker's back...

19:24.391 --> 19:25.556
I know.

19:25.592 --> 19:27.957
Honey, I'm back on TV.

19:27.992 --> 19:29.725
No, Billy,
that's Tom Tucker.

19:29.761 --> 19:31.192
Aw.

19:31.227 --> 19:33.026
What's going on?

19:33.062 --> 19:35.395
Don't worry about it,
just get those pants off.

19:35.430 --> 19:37.929
Oh, your hair is amazing.

19:37.965 --> 19:40.864
Tell us, crazy person,
why are you doing all this?

19:40.899 --> 19:42.065
I'll tell you why.

19:42.100 --> 19:44.833
I'm doing this because
I ruined a guy's life...

19:44.869 --> 19:46.333
and I feel awful about it.

19:46.368 --> 19:49.735
It's the only thing I can think
of to make things right.

19:51.405 --> 19:54.271
Well, whoever this guy is,
I'm sure he appreciates

19:54.306 --> 19:55.605
what you're trying
to do for him.

19:55.640 --> 19:58.039
I think I speak for all
our viewers when I say,

19:58.075 --> 19:59.573
don't do this.

19:59.609 --> 20:00.941
Please.

20:00.977 --> 20:02.475
Come down off
this ledge with me.

20:02.511 --> 20:04.109
You got it.

20:04.145 --> 20:07.478
If that's what the most trusted
newsman in Quahog wants.

20:09.448 --> 20:10.413
Aah! Pigeon!

20:12.583 --> 20:13.548
It's fine.

20:13.583 --> 20:14.582
He landed on people.

20:20.263 --> 20:22.396
Well, I'm glad your
crazy stunt worked out

20:22.431 --> 20:24.496
and Tom Tucker is back
at Channel Five.

20:24.531 --> 20:25.497
Yeah, apparently,

20:25.532 --> 20:26.730
when he interviewed me
up on that roof,

20:26.766 --> 20:29.232
the ratings were so huge,
they made him anchor again.

20:29.267 --> 20:30.766
That's great
to hear, because...

20:30.801 --> 20:33.601
Lois! Lois!

20:33.636 --> 20:35.136
I-Is somebody
calling my name?

20:35.171 --> 20:36.969
Lois!

20:37.004 --> 20:38.103
I don't think so, no.

20:38.139 --> 20:39.671
Lois, I'm rich!

20:39.706 --> 20:41.706
Now I think I do
hear something.

20:41.741 --> 20:43.306
I should probably
go see what he wants.

20:43.341 --> 20:47.475
I know I'm a nerd, but I have,
like, a thing for rich guys.

20:49.678 --> 20:52.477
Oh, boy, she's getting
in his helicopter.

20:52.513 --> 20:53.679
Fa-doo, fa-doo,
fa-doo, fa-doo,

20:53.714 --> 20:55.812
fa-doo, fa-doo,
fa-doo, fa-doo, fa-doo...

20:55.847 --> 20:58.814
Well, I'm big enough
to admit when I'm wrong.

21:01.340 --> 21:07.837
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru